        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Reject nonfinite Kimi K2 usage values",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- reject non-finite Kimi K2 credit and average-token values from JSON or headers\n- keep missing/malformed values on the existing zero-or-nil fallback path\n- allow an injected HTTP transport for deterministic production-path validation\n- cover NaN, infinity, and overflow numeric strings\n\n## Production-path proof\n\nA temporary executable linked against `CodexBarCore` called the public fetcher with an in-memory HTTP response:\n\n```text\nconsumed=0.0 remaining=0.0 average=nil\nfinite=true\n```\n\nThe temporary proof target was removed after the run. No live credentials were used.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter KimiK2UsageFetcherTests` (7 passed)\n- `make check` (SwiftFormat clean; SwiftLint 0 violations; final host cache plist write blocked by sandbox permissions)\n- `git diff --check`",
